                <pb facs="0640" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/152.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Leishman to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-04-23"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 23, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Leishman says Constantinople is surrounded by besieging forces whose
                    headquarters are at St. Malo, Stefano, where Parliament is sitting. Says there
                    are no disorders in the city, but great uneasiness prevails, and that the
                    situation in Adana and Aleppo district remains bad and massacres continue in
                    many cities, according to report of consul. Missionaries at Hadjin are greatly
                    alarmed, and while no disturbances have occurred the place is menaced. Says the
                    movement does not seem to be directed against foreigners, whose greatest danger
                    is being caught in a melee or in harboring refugees.</p>
            </div>
